{"version":"1","id":"tenderlove","handle":"tenderlove","name":"Tenderlove Making","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/87e9008633884d539ab3b48a87c53613","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-3.3574,"y":-1.4691,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":13,"newest_post_at":"2026-05-06T00:00:00.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2022-12-07T00:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.076923,"avg_read_time":5.461538,"summary_length_avg":338.0,"title_length_avg":29.307692,"title_length_var":58.213018,"tag_entropy":2.232056,"tag_diversity":1.0,"top_tag_share":0.230769,"avg_upvotes":1.692308,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.076923,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.086957,"zero_engagement_share":0.692308,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.073028,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.083333},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-1.1765,3.8088],"cadence_depth":[-9.2794,-1.0882],"hype_variety":[-7.5,-8.1912],"title_style":[7.8088,-2.8382]},"top_tags":[["ruby",8],["performance",3],["hardware",2],["mac",2],["security",1],["open-source",1],["rails",1],["iot",1]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Can Bundler Be as Fast as uv?","Using Serial Ports with Ruby","Monkey Patch Detection in Ruby"],"outlier":["Bitmap Matrix and Undirected Graphs in Ruby"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"dSDZam56T","title":"Pixoo64 Ruby Client","url":"https://tenderlovemaking.com/2026/01/01/pixoo64-ruby-client/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/pixoo64-ruby-client-dsdzam56t","summary":"A Ruby client library was created for the Pixoo64 LED display, which connects via WiFi and exposes an HTTP API. The library includes functionality to convert PNG files to the display's binary format and can be configured to fetch and display real-time data like PM2.5 and CO2 levels from remote servers.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6ad2dc4f4931c801ff3a395e4e5ca429?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"wDphoWRvn","title":"Cat photography session","url":"https://tenderlovemaking.com/shots/2025-12-30-cat-pics/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/tenderlove-making-wdphowrvn","summary":"A brief personal post sharing that the author took some cat photographs in the evening. No technical content or development-related information is provided.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ffbac4227b2a3e51963d1744282163a3?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-12-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"WePUBZ6sj","title":"Can Bundler Be as Fast as uv?","url":"https://tenderlovemaking.com/2025/12/29/can-bundler-be-as-fast-as-uv/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/can-bundler-be-as-fast-as-uv--wepubz6sj","summary":"Bundler can achieve performance comparable to uv without rewriting in Rust by addressing architectural bottlenecks. Key improvements include decoupling gem downloading from installation to enable parallel downloads, implementing a global cache with hardlinks, and optimizing version comparison using integer encoding. The main challenges are backwards compatibility and navigating legacy codebases, not fundamental technical limitations. Most performance gains come from what the tool doesn't do rather than the implementation language, with opportunities for parallelizing IO-bound operations and eliminating unnecessary sequential dependencies during installation.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--VDukGCjf--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2002","num_upvotes":16,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2025-12-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"89292oMpd","title":"Apple Photos app Corrupts Images","url":"https://tenderlovemaking.com/2025/09/17/apple-photos-app-corrupts-images/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/apple-photos-app-corrupts-images-89292ompd","summary":"Apple Photos app randomly corrupts RAW and JPEG images during import from cameras, with corruption rates reaching up to 30% of imported files. The issue persists across different hardware configurations and appears to be a software bug. A detailed investigation reveals that corrupted files have identical sizes but different checksums compared to originals. The author switched to Darktable for importing and processing before transferring to Photos app as a workaround.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ba22b9fd62553e928ad2ac030a91bfb3?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"lzpF3x68D","title":"File preallocation on macOS in Ruby","url":"https://tenderlovemaking.com/2025/09/10/file-preallocation-on-macos-in-ruby/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/file-preallocation-on-macos-in-ruby-lzpf3x68d","summary":"Demonstrates how to preallocate files on macOS using Ruby's fcntl gem to optimize large file operations. The technique uses the F_PREALLOCATE flag with specific struct formatting to reserve disk space before writing, potentially improving performance for operations like tar file extraction. Includes working code example and notes that a custom fcntl gem branch is required.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--qPvKM23u--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2009","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-09-10T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"T2B5DKD2I","title":"Monkey Patch Detection in Ruby","url":"https://tenderlovemaking.com/2024/10/16/monkey-patch-detection-in-ruby/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/monkey-patch-detection-in-ruby-t2b5dkd2i","summary":"CRuby can detect and de-optimize itself when methods such as Array#max are monkey patched. This involves maintaining a method table and setting flags in a global variable when important methods are redefined, ensuring optimized paths are avoided. This mechanism helps maintain performance and correctness in the presence of monkey patches.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--VDukGCjf--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2002","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-10-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"9rVNNL6qw","title":"Eliminating Intermediate Array Allocations","url":"https://tenderlovemaking.com/2024/09/29/eliminating-intermediate-array-allocations/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/eliminating-intermediate-array-allocations-9rvnnl6qw","summary":"The post discusses methods to eliminate intermediate array allocations in Ruby, emphasizing that not all operations involve memory allocation. Examples and insights into Ruby's compiler optimizations are provided, showing how certain patterns like `[x, y].max` can be efficient. It underscores the importance of understanding allocation to write performant Ruby code, and touches on the limitations of linting tools in enforcing performance rules.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--CxzD6vbw--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2005","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"7fObx4qo8","title":"Using Serial Ports with Ruby","url":"http://tenderlovemaking.com/2024/02/16/using-serial-ports-with-ruby.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/using-serial-ports-with-ruby-7fobx4qo8","summary":"Learn how to use serial ports with Ruby using the UART gem. Discover how to get the hardware version and receive live updates from a device connected via a serial port.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--qPvKM23u--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2009","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-02-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"9iwykNIs0","title":"Fast Tokenizers with StringScanner","url":"http://tenderlovemaking.com/2023/09/02/fast-tokenizers-with-stringscanner.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/fast-tokenizers-with-stringscanner-9iwyknis0","summary":"The lexer is just breaking down an input string in to a series of tokens. It's the parser\u2019s job to interpret those tokens. Today we\u2019re going to look at a few tricks for speeding up a very basic lexer.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--CxzD6vbw--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2005","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"P6zSrulhE","title":"Bitmap Matrix and Undirected Graphs in Ruby","url":"http://tenderlovemaking.com/2023/03/19/bitmap-matrix-and-undirected-graphs-in-ruby.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/bitmap-matrix-and-undirected-graphs-in-ruby-p6zsrulhe","summary":"Bitmap Matrix and Undirected Graphs in Ruby 2023-03-19 @ 12:12. I made a bitmap matrix implementation that I like, but I think the code is too trivial to put in a Gem. Copying the matrix is trivial because we just have to dup the string.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--P4t4XyoV--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2001","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["docusaurus","abinoda","patkua","benkuhn","daily_js"],"opposite_handles":["tbpn","alexfinn","felixrieseberg","ryolu_","kloss_xyz"],"similar":[{"id":"docusaurus","handle":"docusaurus","name":"Docusaurus","is_squad":false,"x":-3.3875,"y":-1.5694,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":26,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/5f3722c0b00a4f58a4d509e26dc22e53","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.225433,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.019231,"avg_read_time":4.346154,"tag_diversity":0.615385},"top_tags_preview":[["docusaurus",25],["webdev",16],["react",7]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[8.1029,4.3235],"cadence_depth":[-7.3382,-3.8235],"hype_variety":[4.5882,-8.7794],"title_style":[-5.3382,-1.2059]}},{"id":"abinoda","handle":"abinoda","name":"Software Engineering Research","is_squad":false,"x":-3.5424,"y":-1.3302,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":102,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t